WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.132
Part three. Finding a job, and handing the homework over.

00:00:04.432 --> 00:00:08.939
Every application you take seriously starts with the same unpaid hour.

00:00:08.939 --> 00:00:13.638
Reading the posting properly. Working out what the company actually does.

00:00:13.638 --> 00:00:16.535
Digging out the salary, the skills they want,

00:00:16.535 --> 00:00:18.660
and who you should be writing to.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:23.230
Save the job here instead, and that whole list moves across to the app.

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:26.192
You spend your time applying, not researching.

00:00:26.492 --> 00:00:30.752
Search from inside the app. Describe the job in your own words.

00:00:31.052 --> 00:00:36.023
Or search the live web right there. Real results, current listings.

00:00:36.323 --> 00:00:38.339
Open any careers page you like.

00:00:38.339 --> 00:00:40.551
The robot button travels with you,

00:00:40.551 --> 00:00:44.193
so it is sitting right there on the employer's own site.

00:00:44.493 --> 00:00:48.203
Tap it, hit Fetch job, and it reads the whole page.

00:00:48.503 --> 00:00:52.751
The posting lands in your saved list, scored against your résumé.

00:00:53.051 --> 00:00:55.264
Next, what it does with all that.

00:00:55.264 --> 00:00:58.685
It reads the role, goes and researches the company,

00:00:58.685 --> 00:01:00.697
and writes the letter for you.

